--
^warning: ignoring
--
The virtual pointer of D's second A subobject (through C) held a table of
type virtual_table::A, which the conversion from C to the virtual base V
read as a virtual_table::C, out of bounds, so V::g's dispatch through C
was wrong.  The table of a repeated subobject is now a copy of the direct
base's whole table (C's), made also when the class has virtual bases and
no overriders, and the pointer points into it along the same members.
